  "body": "## Description\n\nThe `executeDeposit` function in the HypoVault contract lacks slippage protection, allowing users to receive fewer shares than expected for their deposited assets. This vulnerability stems from the two-phase deposit system where users have no control over the exchange rate determination.\n\n**File:** `src/HypoVault.sol`  \n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Requests a deposit of assets.\n/// @param assets The amount of assets to deposit\nfunction requestDeposit(uint128 assets) external {\n    uint256 currentEpoch = depositEpoch; // Get current deposit epoch\n\n    queuedDeposit[msg.sender][currentEpoch] += assets; // Add to user's queued deposits\n\n    depositEpochState[currentEpoch].assetsDeposited += assets; // Update total deposits for epoch\n\n    SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(underlyingToken, msg.sender, address(this), assets); // Transfer tokens to vault\n\n    emit DepositRequested(msg.sender, assets); // Emit deposit requested event\n}\n```\nand the execute function: \n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Converts an active pending deposit into shares.\n/// @param user The address that requested the deposit\n/// @param epoch The epoch in which the deposit was requested\nfunction executeDeposit(address user, uint256 epoch) external {\n    if (epoch >= depositEpoch) revert EpochNotFulfilled(); // Check if epoch has been fulfilled\n\n    uint256 queuedDepositAmount = queuedDeposit[user][epoch]; // Get user's queued deposit amount\n    \n    queuedDeposit[user][epoch] = 0; // Clear the queued deposit\n\n    DepositEpochState memory _depositEpochState = depositEpochState[epoch]; // Get epoch state\n\n    uint256 userAssetsDeposited = Math.mulDiv(\n        queuedDepositAmount, // User's deposit amount\n        _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled, // Total assets fulfilled in epoch\n        _depositEpochState.assetsDeposited // Total assets deposited in epoch\n    ); // Calculate user's fulfilled deposit amount\n\n    uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(\n        userAssetsDeposited, // User's fulfilled assets\n        _depositEpochState.sharesReceived, // Total shares minted for epoch\n        _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled // Total assets fulfilled in epoch\n    ); // Calculate shares user should receive\n\n    // shares from pending deposits are already added to the supply at the start of every new epoch\n    _mintVirtual(user, sharesReceived); // Mint shares to user\n\n    userBasis[user] += userAssetsDeposited; // Update user's cost basis\n   \n    queuedDeposit[user][epoch] = 0; // Clear queued deposit again (redundant)\n\n    uint256 assetsRemaining = queuedDepositAmount - userAssetsDeposited; // Calculate unfulfilled assets\n\n    // move remainder of deposit to next epoch -- unfulfilled assets in this epoch will be handled in the next epoch\n    if (assetsRemaining > 0) queuedDeposit[user][epoch + 1] += uint128(assetsRemaining); // Move remaining assets to next epoch\n\n    emit DepositExecuted(user, userAssetsDeposited, sharesReceived, epoch); // Emit deposit executed event\n}\n```\n\n**Related Function:** `fulfillDeposits` \n\n```solidity\nfunction fulfillDeposits(\n    uint256 assetsToFulfill, // Amount of assets to fulfill\n    bytes memory managerInput // Optional input for accountant\n) external onlyManager {\n    uint256 currentEpoch = depositEpoch; // Get current deposit epoch\n\n    DepositEpochState memory epochState = depositEpochState[currentEpoch]; // Get current epoch state\n\n    uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +\n        1 - // Add 1 to avoid division by zero\n        epochState.assetsDeposited - // Subtract pending deposits\n        reservedWithdrawalAssets; // Subtract reserved withdrawal assets\n\n    uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply; // Get current total supply\n\n    uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(assetsToFulfill, _totalSupply, totalAssets); // Calculate shares to mint\n\n    // ... rest of function updates epoch state and total supply\n}\n```\n\n## Impact\n\nMEV bots can sandwich the `fulfillDeposits()` call to manipulate the exchange rate. Users have **zero control** over when their deposits are fulfilled\n\n- The exchange rate is determined entirely by the manager's timing of `fulfillDeposits()`\n- Users may receive significantly fewer shares than expected due to:\n  - Market volatility between deposit request and fulfillment\n  - Manager's strategic timing of fulfillment\n  - NAV calculation manipulation\n\n## Attack Scenarios\n\n1. User calls `requestDeposit(1000 USDC)`\n2. MEV bot front-runs with large deposit to inflate NAV\n3. Manager calls `fulfillDeposits()` with inflated NAV\n4. User's `executeDeposit()` receives fewer shares due to inflated exchange rate\n5. MEV bot back-runs with withdrawal to profit\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAdd slippage protection to the `requestDeposit` function by including a minimum expected shares parameter:\n\n```solidity\n/// @notice Requests a deposit of assets with slippage protection.\n/// @param assets The amount of assets to deposit\n/// @param minSharesExpected Minimum shares the user expects to receive\nfunction requestDeposit(uint128 assets, uint256 minSharesExpected) external {\n    uint256 currentEpoch = depositEpoch; // Get current deposit epoch\n\n    queuedDeposit[msg.sender][currentEpoch] += assets; // Add to user's queued deposits\n\n    depositEpochState[currentEpoch].assetsDeposited += assets; // Update total deposits for epoch\n\n    // Store the minimum shares expected for this deposit\n    depositMinShares[msg.sender][currentEpoch] = minSharesExpected;\n\n    SafeTransferLib.safeTransferFrom(underlyingToken, msg.sender, address(this), assets); // Transfer tokens to vault\n\n    emit DepositRequested(msg.sender, assets); // Emit deposit requested event\n}\n```\n\nThen modify the `executeDeposit` function to check against the stored minimum:\n\n```solidity\nfunction executeDeposit(address user, uint256 epoch) external {\n    if (epoch >= depositEpoch) revert EpochNotFulfilled();\n\n    uint256 queuedDepositAmount = queuedDeposit[user][epoch];\n    uint256 minSharesExpected = depositMinShares[user][epoch];\n    \n    queuedDeposit[user][epoch] = 0;\n    depositMinShares[user][epoch] = 0; // Clear the stored minimum\n\n    DepositEpochState memory _depositEpochState = depositEpochState[epoch];\n\n    uint256 userAssetsDeposited = Math.mulDiv(\n        queuedDepositAmount,\n        _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled,\n        _depositEpochState.assetsDeposited\n    );\n\n    uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(\n        userAssetsDeposited,\n        _depositEpochState.sharesReceived,\n        _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled\n    );\n\n    // Add slippage protection\n    if (sharesReceived < minSharesExpected) revert InsufficientSharesReceived();\n\n    _mintVirtual(user, sharesReceived);\n    userBasis[user] += userAssetsDeposited;\n\n    emit DepositExecuted(user, userAssetsDeposited, sharesReceived, epoch);\n}\n```",
